  "recipeCuisine": "Italy",
  "name": "Pesto Genoese",
  "text": "Pesto Genoese\n\nPreparation time: 15 minutes\n\nCooking time: 15 minutes\n\nYield: 4\n\nIngredients\n\n250 g (8 oz) potatoes (peeled and thinly sliced),\n\n150 g (5 oz) green beans,\n\n75 g (3 oz) basil leaves,\n\n25 g (1 oz) pine nuts,\n\n2 garlic cloves (crushed),\n\n2 tbsp freshly grated Parmesan cheese (plus extra to serve),\n\n1 tbsp freshly grated pecorino cheese,\n\n3 tbsp olive oil.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Cook the potatoes in a large saucepan for 10 minutes. Then add the beans and cook for a further 5 minutes.\n\n2. Meanwhile blend the basil, pine nuts, and garlic, in a food processor until the mixture forms a thick paste. Add the cheeses and process briefly, then, with the motor still running, pour in the oil in a thin steady stream.\n\n3. Drain the vegetables, reserving 2 tbsp of the cooking water. Return the vegetables to the pan, and stir in the pesto sauce, adding the reserved water to loosen the mixture. Serve with the extra Parmesan cheese.",
  "prepTime": "PT15M",
  "cookTime": "PT15M",
  "recipeYield": "4",
